WHAT "CURRICULUM CONTENT" MEANS HERE

1. The numbered content trees: 00_START_HERE/ through 14_Tracks/, and 99_Archive/.
   Exception: 13_Faculty_Resources/_automation/ is build and validation code, not content.
2. The root registries that carry curriculum material, for example topic_meta.json,
   question_bank.json, curriculum.json, communication_cases.json, reasoning_cases.json,
   reasoning_cases_resident.json, longitudinal_case.json, family_systems_scenarios.json,
   pairings.json, evidence_registry.json and evidence_annotations.json. (Their paired
   *.schema.json files are code.)
3. The learner-facing text in _prototypes/, such as the scenario and standardized-patient
   case packs (*.pack.json) and the text of the tools that ship to learners.
4. The built learner pages of both sites (the output of
   13_Faculty_Resources/_automation/site_build/build_and_check.sh), and the
   curriculum-review transcripts in docs/curriculum-review/, which are copies of them.

Some files mix the two. The single-file HTML clinical tools contain both program logic
and teaching text. In those files the program logic is code under the MIT License (see
LICENSE), and the teaching text, cases, questions, feedback and other educational
material are content under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

